sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Scheduler
    participant W as Web / API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant R as Outbox relay
    participant N as Notification Delivery
    participant P as Provider adapter

    U->>W: Publish schedule
    activate W
    W->>DB: BEGIN
    W->>DB: create schedule_version + assignments
    W->>DB: INSERT outbox_events (SchedulePublished)
    W->>DB: INSERT audit_events
    W->>DB: COMMIT
    deactivate W
    W-->>U: Published (notifications will follow)

    Note over DB,R: Commit is the only guarantee needed.<br/>A provider outage cannot roll this back.

    R->>DB: claim outbox row
    R->>N: domain event
    N->>N: resolve intents (affected memberships)
    N->>N: render per recipient, per channel
    N->>P: dispatch (idempotency key)
    P-->>N: outcome
    N->>DB: record delivery_attempt
    Note over N,DB: failure -> backoff + jitter -> dead-letter.<br/>Never a silent discard.
